# genesis/seeder — corpus seeding

What belongs here: the seeder's TypeScript sources and vitest specs (`src/`), its diagnostics and
spikes (`scripts/`), and the declared inputs it reads, such as `stakes-declaration.json`. The
root interface is `just seed validate|apply|stats`. `src/seed.ts` is the focused entry point for
specialist runs.

There is deliberately no seed dry-run. The retired `--dry-run` and `--validate-only` aliases were
ignored and could write. Do not add a preview mode until the seeder has a tested non-writing
execution path; `just seed validate` is the non-writing check.

`covers: subtree` is a considered ownership claim with no edit-time rule. A tool run from this
directory that writes its own `.claude/` state here is a stray, handled by `.gitignore`, not by
this manifest.
